<title>UK: UK grain traders bid for free market soft wheat.</title>
<headline>UK grain traders bid for free market soft wheat.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain traders bid for licences to export free market wheat at the weekly European Union (EU) tender on Thursday, the UK Intervention Board for Agricultural Produce said.</p>
<p>The board could give no further details as there were less than three bids.</p>
<p>There was no interest for free market barley, the board added.</p>
<p>All bids will be considered at Thursday's weekly EU cereals management committee meeting.</p>
<p>--Jim Ballantyne, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8062</p>
